<title>USA: FSA qualifies eight muni issues for bond insurance.</title>
<headline>FSA qualifies eight muni issues for bond insurance.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Financial Security Assurance said it has qualified for bond insurance the following eight municipal issues scheduled for competitive sale today.</p>
<p>--Washington Elementary School District #6, Ariz., School Improvement, $34.825 million.</p>
<p>--Clinton Prairie Sch., Ind., $1.9 million mortgage bonds.</p>
<p>--Gloucester, Mass., General Obligations (GOs), $14.575 million.</p>
<p>--Marion, Mass., $1.795 million muni purpose loan.</p>
<p>--Park Ridge, N.J., General Improvement, $2.935 million.</p>
<p>--Corning City, N.Y., School District, $3.5 million.</p>
<p>--Rockland County, N.Y., $19.8 million GOs.</p>
<p>--Florida State Board Of Regent, Revenues, $45.395 million.</p>
<p>--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650</p>
</text>
